      {
        "id": 115232,
        "name": "lutherbellhendricksv",
        "username": "lutherbellhendricksv",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lutherbellhendricksv/{size}/2350_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-18T16:26:03.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Acefury.eq\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/acefury.eq/48/2078_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Acefury.eq:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Should Becon's innate ability be unlimited? It does not list the unlimited trait, but it's almost identical to other hersos innate abilities that do show the trait (ex. ra)&nbsp;i ask ask bc we were playing a game where baron blade stripped the power cards from the heroes. Ra could still shoot twice but Becon could not, the Becon player found it extreamly infair.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Only abilities labeled Unlimited are naturally Unlimited. This isn't an oversight for Beacon, it's a boon for Ra (and Tachyon). If Beacon wanted to spend another action to do more damage, she could of course Aim before using her single attack.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:47:21.081Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 11017,
        "topic_slug": "beacons-innate-ability-question",
        "display_username": "lutherbellhendricksv",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": true,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "[quote=\"Acefury.eq\"]\n\nShould Becon&#39;s innate ability be unlimited? It does not list the unlimited trait, but it&#39;s almost identical to other hersos innate abilities that do show the trait (ex. ra)&nbsp;i ask ask bc we were playing a game where baron blade stripped the power cards from the heroes. Ra could still shoot twice but Becon could not, the Becon player found it extreamly infair.&nbsp;\n\n[/quote]\n\nOnly abilities labeled Unlimited are naturally Unlimited. This isn&#39;t an oversight for Beacon, it&#39;s a boon for Ra (and Tachyon). If Beacon wanted to spend another action to do more damage, she could of course Aim before using her single attack.\n",
        "actions_summary": [],
        "moderator": false,
        "admin": false,
        "staff": false,
        "user_id": 4521,
        "hidden": false,
        "trust_level": 1,
